      "transformer": "reject_bias_mode dominant (9/10), full breakdown: {'intermediate_shortcut_leaning': 1, 'reject_bias_mode': 9}",
      "mamba": "reject_bias_mode dominant (7/10), full breakdown: {'reject_bias_mode': 7, 'clean_shortcut_mode': 2, 'intermediate_shortcut_leaning': 1}"
    },
    "note_on_rnn_and_mamba_characterization": "RNN and Mamba do NOT show an identical 'split' pattern to each other, despite both being more mixed than LSTM (shortcut-dominant) and Transformer (reject-bias-dominant): RNN leans shortcut-majority ({'reject_bias_mode': 3, 'clean_shortcut_mode': 6, 'intermediate_shortcut_leaning': 1}), while Mamba leans reject-bias-majority ({'reject_bias_mode': 7, 'clean_shortcut_mode': 2, 'intermediate_shortcut_leaning': 1}) -- reported precisely here rather than smoothed into a single 'both split evenly' characterization."
  },
